# Centralised App Assets (Common Assets)

## Core Principle
All app assets (fonts, graphics, icons) served from single centralized location shared across Noble Architecture applications. Assets are static files on GitHub Pages, referenced via relative paths only.

## Hard Constraints
- **Read-Only at runtime** - GitHub Pages serves static content only
- Never duplicate assets into individual app directories
- Always use relative paths for portability
- Asset paths must work identically in local and production

---

# Locations & Path Mapping

## Paths
**Local:** `D:\WE10_--_Public-Repo_--_Live-Website\na-apps\01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets\`
**GitHub:** `https://www.noble-architecture.com/na-apps/01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets/`
**Relative from Core App:** `../../01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets/`

Local structure after `D:\WE10_--_Public-Repo_--_Live-Website\` mirrors GitHub structure after `https://www.noble-architecture.com/`.

## Directory Structure

```
01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets/
├── NaApps__CommonFonts/          (OpenSans: Regular, Bold, Light, Medium, SemiBold)
├── NaApps__CommonGraphics/       (Logos, Signatures, Brand Graphics)
└── NaApps__CommonIcons/          (Favicons: ICO, PNG, SVG variants)
```

